  "final_message": "I put `channel` back everywhere I removed it. Typecheck passes and all 39 unit tests pass. I couldn't run the ARCH-4 check itself, because it isn't defined in this repo. I haven't committed anything.\n\nYour premise was wrong: `analytics-ingest` still requires `OrderPlaced.channel`, as an enum of `web|store|marketplace`. The consumer contract lives outside this repo, so I had no way to see that when I made the change.\n\nI couldn't run `git revert --no-commit HEAD` because it was blocked. So I reversed the edits by hand instead. The working tree now matches the `base` commit (2007adf), as far as `git diff --stat` shows. The `gen` commit (d22da95) still contains the removal, and my restoring edits sit on top of it as uncommitted changes.\n\nIf you do want `channel` gone, the order would be:\n1. Have `analytics-ingest` stop requiring it.\n2. Re-run my removal.\n3. Probably bump `OrderPlaced.schemaVersion` to 4, since dropping a field breaks consumers that still require it.\n\nI can redo the removal once the `analytics-ingest` side is done.",
